{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2387 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "701f8e3586924ca6d858ff6d15da985a239a5b9e6949659ba85e439f86f3c26e" :edb/db-before-t 2386 :edb/db-after-t 2387 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535699 50 #inst "2026-10-09T05:28:37.982Z" 13194139535699 true] [17592186157329 1020 #edb/ref 17592186362097 13194139535699 true] [17592186157329 1020 #edb/ref 17592186362104 13194139535699 true] [17592186362097 1017 #edb/ref 17592186362098 13194139535699 true] [17592186362097 1089 "q-156192" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362097 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535699 true] [17592186362097 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{8}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=A,$ what is the value of ${\\int }_{-8}^{0}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x?$" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362097 1113 #uuid "456bde2b-ef1e-54aa-8da0-4de187218c6c" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362097 1145 "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡((-x)^{3}) \\\\  & =(-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3}) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-8}^{8}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the adjacent intervals rule for integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-8}^{8}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-8}^{0}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{8}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-8}^{0}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+A & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-8}^{0}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =-A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362098 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362099 13194139535699 true] [17592186362098 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362100 13194139535699 true] [17592186362098 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362101 13194139535699 true] [17592186362098 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362102 13194139535699 true] [17592186362098 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362103 13194139535699 true] [17592186362098 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535699 true] [17592186362098 1041 "selection" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362098 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362101 13194139535699 true] [17592186362098 1110 #uuid "ab8e5837-811c-5c91-a54d-f7aaf6cfb9ac" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362099 1034 "2A" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362099 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535699 true] [17592186362099 1111 #uuid "7c97e840-f296-503d-88e5-9cf4fc8a4408" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362100 1034 "A" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362100 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535699 true] [17592186362100 1111 #uuid "404a9778-2b59-5121-8fbb-9423bf284569" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362101 1034 "-A" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362101 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535699 true] [17592186362101 1111 #uuid "652acd58-20e1-5135-b4af-84b85fa6aabd" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362102 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}A" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362102 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535699 true] [17592186362102 1111 #uuid "7791ebe8-5281-5de1-931d-24d8361211ba" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362103 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}A" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362103 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535699 true] [17592186362103 1111 #uuid "d92be062-f23a-5ae3-9bab-6ce2dec4818c" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362104 1017 #edb/ref 17592186362105 13194139535699 true] [17592186362104 1089 "q-316128" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362104 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535699 true] [17592186362104 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{4}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=p,$ express the value of ${\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x$ in terms of $p.$\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362104 1113 #uuid "ad0b6114-b30d-54df-8d07-1628e7d83ec4" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362104 1145 "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x),$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x).$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x){e}^{(-x)^{2}+1} \\\\  & =-x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{4}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the adjacent intervals rule for integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{4}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x+p & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =-p.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362105 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362106 13194139535699 true] [17592186362105 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535699 true] [17592186362105 1041 "field-1" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362105 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362106 13194139535699 true] [17592186362105 1110 #uuid "9c041021-1d80-557e-893e-8b852062da80" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362106 1034 "-p" 13194139535699 true] [17592186362106 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535699 true] [17592186362106 1111 #uuid "4be6f67a-d2ec-5bc9-a9cd-458f72abdb7a" 13194139535699 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-156192" 17592186362097 "q-156192/selection" 17592186362098 "q-156192/selection/2975a59a267852917cc6f11a023dfb0a3a74e161efa53fb66f82